rictions will be lifted at 12pm on Monday, November 17, 2025."}]},{"id":"PS 362","title":"Qualitative Research on Politics","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"78726","code":"A","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":750,"end":830,"location":"219 David Kinley Hall","instructors":["Khoury, R"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Major restrictions will be lifted by noon on Monday, November 16, 2026."}]},{"id":"PS 372","title":"Modern Political Theory","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"46285","code":"A","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":660,"end":740,"location":"223 Gregory Hall","instructors":["Erlenbusch-Anderson, V"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Major restrictions will be lifted by noon on Monday, November 16, 2026."}]},{"id":"PS 373","title":"Democratic Theory","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"48895","code":"A","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":750,"end":830,"location":"212 David Kinley Hall","instructors":["Seitz, S"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Major restrictions will be lifted by noon on Monday, November 16, 2026."}]},{"id":"PS 377","title":"Topics Contemp Pol Theory","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"39854","code":"ER","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":930,"end":1010,"location":"138 Henry Administration Bldg","instructors":["Rota, E"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"This course examines the evolution of neofascist ideologies, movements, and regimes from 1945 to the present. We will analyze the ideological foundations of neofascism, the role of clandestine networks, and the impact of far-right extremism on contemporary politics. We will also discuss legal, philosophical, and historical debates over neofascist movements. This course involves analysis of primary sources from figures like Julius Evola, Aleksandr Dugin, Francis Parker Yockey, and Savitri Devi, as well as recent scholarship on the topic. (Meets with ITAL 390). Major restrictions will be lifted by noon on Monday, November 16, 2026."}]},{"id":"PS 382","title":"Intl Political Economy","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"43210","code":"A","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["M","W"],"start":900,"end":980,"location":"1002 Lincoln Hall","instructors":["Obrien Udry, C"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Major restrictions will be lifted by noon on Monday, November 16, 2026."}]},{"id":"PS 389","title":"International Communications","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"48447","code":"A","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["M","W"],"start":660,"end":740,"location":"307 Gregory Hall","instructors":["Ciafone, A"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Please note, Thursday will be held online."}]},{"id":"PS 398","title":"Strategic Interntl Relations","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"62312","code":"A","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":660,"end":740,"location":"107 Animal Sciences Laboratory","instructors":["Carroll, R"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Major restrictions will be lifted by noon on Monday, November 16, 2026."}]},{"id":"PS 399","title":"Politics of International Treaties","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"66659","code":"A","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":660,"end":740,"location":"326 David Kinley Hall","instructors":["Dai, X"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Major restrictions will be lifted by noon on Monday, November 16, 2026."}]},{"id":"PS 418","title":"Language & Minorities in Europe","creditHours":"3 OR 4 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"50307","code":